541	    /**
542	     * Builds the customer code assigned to a newly created owner. The code is formatted as
543	     * {@code '<REGION>-<HASH8>'}, where {@code REGION} is the owner's canonical region (see
544	     * {@link Owner#getRegion()}), rendered {@code 'UNKNOWN'} when the owner has no known region,
545	     * and {@code HASH8} is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of the SHA-256 digest over the
546	     * owner's normalized E.164 {@code telephone} concatenated with its {@code lastName}. The code
547	     * carries no sequence number, so two owners sharing a region, telephone and last name resolve to
548	     * the same code. The whole owner is taken so the code is derived from whichever of its fields the
549	     * identity scheme needs.
