779	     * {@code null} email (none was supplied) canonicalizes to {@code null}. Unlike
780	     * {@link #normalizeEmail(String)} no validation is performed, so this can be applied to a
781	     * value read back off an existing owner without risk of rejecting it. This is the single
782	     * definition of email identity: two emails denote the same address exactly when they
783	     * canonicalize to the same value, so an email stored via {@link #normalizeEmail(String)} and
